Template: homelab-postfix-block-link/db_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL host to bootstrap this app's role on:
 Used only once, at first install, to run
 homelab-postfix-block-link-bootstrap-role. Must already have
 homelab-api, homelab-domain-admin, and homelab-block-link installed/
 migrated on it -- this role's grants reach into all three.

Template: homelab-postfix-block-link/pgbouncer_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PgBouncer host to register this app's runtime role with:
 Used only once, at first install. Also written into config.yml's
 database.host, so the milter connects through the pooler -- it sits
 on the hot SMTP delivery path, same reasoning as homelab-postfix's
 own runtime role.

Template: homelab-postfix-block-link/instance_id
Type: string
Default:
Description: Unique identifier for this specific postfix instance (blank = single-instance):
 Only needed when installing on more than one postfix host behind the
 same HAProxy pool (e.g. "ct05", "ct06") -- appends _<value> to this
 app's own Postgres role name, exactly like homelab-postfix's own
 instance_id already does, to give each instance its own credential
 instead of sharing one (a shared role means the LAST install's
 password silently rotates out from under every other already-running
 instance -- found live and fixed for postfix/dovecot/roundcube's own
 roles this project's history, not repeated here).

Template: homelab-postfix-block-link/milter_listen
Type: string
Default: inet:8892@127.0.0.1
Description: Socket for this milter to listen on:
 Sendmail::PMilter connection-descriptor syntax (same style OpenDKIM's
 own Socket directive already uses in this fleet, inet:8891@0.0.0.0) --
 loopback-only by default, since only this host's own Postfix should
 ever speak the milter protocol to it.

Template: homelab-postfix-block-link/public_base_url
Type: string
Default: https://blockemail.test.mailmasker.org
Description: Public URL used in generated links (must match homelab-block-link's own setting):
 NOT auto-synced with homelab-block-link's own identically-named
 config value -- same deliberate "two related settings, kept in sync
 by hand" pattern already used for Roundcube's session_lifetime vs
 homelab-sso's JWT lifetime elsewhere in this project. If
 homelab-block-link's public_base_url ever changes, update this too
 (dpkg-reconfigure homelab-postfix-block-link) or generated links will
 point at the wrong place.

Template: homelab-postfix-block-link/link_ttl_days
Type: string
Default: 90
Description: Days a generated link stays valid (cosmetic hint only):
 The REAL expiry is enforced entirely by homelab-block-link itself
 (its own link_ttl_days). This value only affects what this milter
 writes into block_link.pending_links.expires_at at insert time --
 keep it equal to homelab-block-link's own setting.
